/S /H3
/P 59 0 R
/T (Important: The cleanest design for blank entries is while with an explicit attempts counter. In a for-loop, use a while loop inside each slot or a separate counted-attempt variable; otherwise blank entries consume an attempt. break exits on success, continue skips blank input, and pass is a no-operation placeholder. Loop else runs only when the loop finishes without break.)
/E (Important: The cleanest design for blank entries is while with an explicit attempts counter. In a for-loop, use a while loop inside each slot or a separate counted-attempt variable; otherwise blank entries consume an attempt. break exits on success, continue skips blank input, and pass is a no-operation placeholder. Loop else runs only when the loop finishes without break.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [46]
>>
endobj
